module Main
import Std.Base

-- Value-CAF referenced from an arity>0 function (F2 regression). 'theList' is a
-- 0-arity top-level bind whose body is a boxed value (a Cons spine); it is forced
-- once at load time and lives for the module's lifetime (an immortal value-CAF,
-- counted in the baseline). 'useList' is an arity>0 function whose body
-- DEREFERENCES that CAF. The bug: 'reserveStatic' reserves a static placeholder
-- cell per bind and closures capture the knotted env mapping each CAF's Unique to
-- its reserved static address; the CAF (otherwise) branch of 'installBinds' only
-- refined the accumulator env with the forced result and NEVER wrote it back into
-- the reserved static cell. A function closure captures the UNREFINED knotEnv, so
-- 'useList' dereferences the never-overwritten placeholder NCon
-- "<uninstalled-global>" --- crashing with NonExhaustiveCase (sumList's case has
-- no arm for the placeholder constructor) or yielding a silently wrong value. The
-- fix writes the forced CAF result back into the reserved static cell so every
-- captor (incl. forward-referencing function closures) resolves the real value.
data List = Nil | Cons U64 List

theList : List
theList = Cons 1 (Cons 2 Nil)

sumList : List -> U64
sumList xs = case xs of
  Nil       -> 0
  Cons h t  -> h + sumList t

useList : U64 -> U64
useList n = sumList theList

main = useList 10
